PROJECT PURPOSE AND SCOPE

The project ingests reproducible synthetic ride CSV records into a local PySpark/Delta Lake pipeline. It demonstrates data validation and quarantine, UTC event-date partitioning, idempotent immutable-key loads, historical city attributes, reconciliation, logs, tests and separate pruning/compaction/history demonstrations.

It is a local batch-processing prototype, not a production cloud deployment, continuous streaming system, real-time ride application, RAG chatbot or UI dashboard. The pipeline itself does not depend on an LLM API or vector database.

The source contract is ONE IMMUTABLE RECORD PER ride_id. It is not a multi-event status-change stream. Identical replays are accepted without inserting duplicates. A different payload for an existing ride ID is rejected as a conflict, not silently updated or appended as history. If new requirements need corrections or multiple events per ride, explain and design a changed contract explicitly.

